  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Pair each positive odd number through \\(97\\) with the negative even number immediately after it. Every pair equals \\(-1\\). There are \\(98\\div2=49\\) such pairs, and the final \\(99\\) is left over. Thus\n\\[\n(1-2)+(3-4)+\\cdots+(97-98)+99\n=49(-1)+99=50.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(50\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
